1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,441
In this lesson, we'll invite a new team
member, choose what they can see and do,

2
00:00:05,441 --> 00:00:07,603
and add them to a booking calendar.

3
00:00:07,603 --> 00:00:10,939
By the end, your whole team
can work in Kyntlo safely.

4
00:00:11,789 --> 00:00:13,815
Go to Settings, then My Staff.

5
00:00:13,815 --> 00:00:16,989
Here's everyone who can
log in to this account.

6
00:00:16,989 --> 00:00:22,189
Your plan sets how many users you can
have: up to 3 on Starter, 10 on Growth,

7
00:00:22,189 --> 00:00:23,134
and 25 on Pro.

8
00:00:23,134 --> 00:00:25,160
Give everyone their own login.

9
00:00:25,160 --> 00:00:28,739
Shared logins make it
impossible to see who did what.

10
00:00:29,590 --> 00:00:31,584
Bloom has a new hygienist, Tom.

11
00:00:31,584 --> 00:00:36,152
Click Add Employee, and enter his
first name, last name and work email.

12
00:00:36,152 --> 00:00:40,012
Add his mobile number too, so
calls can be forwarded to him.

13
00:00:40,862 --> 00:00:43,264
Now the important part: permissions.

14
00:00:43,264 --> 00:00:47,334
Each switch turns a part of
Kyntlo on or off for this person.

15
00:00:47,334 --> 00:00:52,338
Tom needs conversations, calendars and
contacts to look after his patients,

16
00:00:52,338 --> 00:00:55,741
but he doesn't need sales
opportunities or reviews.

17
00:00:56,592 --> 00:01:00,065
Payments, marketing, automation
and settings stay off.

18
00:01:00,065 --> 00:01:05,210
And Bulk Actions stays off too, because
it includes exporting your contact list.

19
00:01:05,210 --> 00:01:08,040
Only give that to people
who really need it.

20
00:01:08,040 --> 00:01:11,577
Tom will only ever see the
areas you switch on for him.

21
00:01:12,427 --> 00:01:15,158
Under User Roles, choose Admin or User.

22
00:01:15,158 --> 00:01:20,831
Admins can manage settings and other users,
so keep that for owners and managers.

23
00:01:20,831 --> 00:01:21,812
Tom is a User.

24
00:01:21,812 --> 00:01:24,543
Then switch on Only show assigned data,

25
00:01:24,543 --> 00:01:27,765
so Tom sees just the
patients assigned to him.

26
00:01:28,614 --> 00:01:32,884
Under Call & Voicemail, choose which
business number Tom calls from,

27
00:01:32,884 --> 00:01:37,279
so patients always see the practice
number, never his personal mobile.

28
00:01:37,279 --> 00:01:38,283
Then click Save.

29
00:01:39,135 --> 00:01:42,422
Tom now appears in the list,
with an invitation sent.

30
00:01:42,422 --> 00:01:47,259
He'll get an email to set his own password,
so you never need to share logins.

31
00:01:47,259 --> 00:01:50,670
To change his access later,
just click the pencil icon.

32
00:01:50,670 --> 00:01:54,081
And if someone leaves, delete
their user straight away,

33
00:01:54,081 --> 00:01:56,748
and reassign their
contacts to a colleague.

34
00:01:57,597 --> 00:02:00,284
Finally, let's let patients book with Tom.

35
00:02:00,284 --> 00:02:02,586
Open Calendars in the settings menu.

36
00:02:02,586 --> 00:02:06,360
Each calendar lists the team
members who take its bookings.

37
00:02:06,360 --> 00:02:08,855
Click Team members on Check-up & Clean.

38
00:02:09,705 --> 00:02:11,306
Tick Tom, and click Save.

39
00:02:11,306 --> 00:02:16,303
This is a round robin calendar, so new
check-ups are now shared between James,

40
00:02:16,303 --> 00:02:19,890
Priya and Tom, and only booked
when each person is free.

41
00:02:20,742 --> 00:02:21,800
Here's a pro tip.

42
00:02:21,800 --> 00:02:25,532
Start every new team member
with the least access they need.

43
00:02:25,532 --> 00:02:30,322
It's easy to switch a permission on
later, but much harder to undo a mistake,

44
00:02:30,322 --> 00:02:32,997
like a bulk message
sent to the wrong list.

45
00:02:33,847 --> 00:02:35,050
Your team is set up!

46
00:02:35,050 --> 00:02:36,553
That wraps up Module one.

47
00:02:36,553 --> 00:02:39,018
Next, we'll learn to read your dashboard,

48
00:02:39,018 --> 00:02:41,784
so you always know how
your business is doing.

49
00:02:41,784 --> 00:02:42,626
See you there.
